<title>HONG KONG: HK Building &amp; Loan 1996 net up 6.82 pct.</title>
<headline>HK Building &amp; Loan 1996 net up 6.82 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   20.0   vs 19.0 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    7.0    vs 6.7 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    45.33  vs 42.43</p>
<p>    Turnover		     102.78 vs 91.19</p>
<p>    Company name		 Hong Kong Building and Loan Agency</p>
<p>				     Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 17-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 17</p>
<p>NOTE - Hong Kong Building and Loan provides mortgages to middle income flat owner-occupiers.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings and final dividend have been adjusted to take account of the bonus issue of two-for-one share and also the sub-division of shares of one-into-five shares both effected on June 25, 1996.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is 10 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of three cents) vs 9.7 cents (adjusted).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
